WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:06.240
How did vampires and werewolves stay hidden&nbsp;
for 600 years? What is their bullet budget?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:11.360
Why is it so dark? What's up with the wings?&nbsp;
Is that catsuit even comfortable? These are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:15.040
some of the many questions that need to&nbsp;
be examined from the "Underworld" movies.

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:20.800
The plot of 2012's "Underworld: Awakening,"&nbsp;
hinges on humans discovering the existence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:27.440
of vampires and lycans. Yet, the two supernatural&nbsp;
species existed for centuries prior to humanity's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:31.760
realization. While the first film indicates&nbsp;
that vampires and lycans have attempted to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:36.960
operate in the shadows, it seems impossible that&nbsp;
their conflict has gone unnoticed for so long.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:41.920
In the second film, "Underworld: Evolution,"&nbsp;
Alexander Corvinus, the first immortal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:46.640
indicates he's spent his long life covering&nbsp;
up the indiscretions of the two species his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:50.240
twin sons originated, but it's hard&nbsp;
to believe he never slipped up over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:54.960
the course of the centuries-long bloodshed&nbsp;
between vampires and lycans. Furthermore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.960 --> 00:01:00.960
in modern times vampires' and lycans' use of loud&nbsp;
guns without silencers would make them especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:05.840
likely to attract attention. At a minimum, people&nbsp;
should have noticed during the first "Underworld,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:10.880
as the two groups have an intense gun battle in a&nbsp;
subway catching multiple humans in the crossfire.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:15.760
In the mythology of "Underworld,"&nbsp;
Kate Beckinsale's Selene and Scott&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:19.360
Speedman's Michael are supposed&nbsp;
to be supernatural star-crossed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:24.960
lovers. As Michael goes from human to lycan to&nbsp;
lycan-vampire hybrid throughout the first film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:29.760
he and Selene are also supposed to be falling for&nbsp;
each other. While the plot of the film makes this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:35.680
clear, Beckinsale and Speedman as actors do not.&nbsp;
Theirs is supposed to be an Earth-shattering love,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:38.800
Instead, their romance is&nbsp;
about as sexy as a damp towel.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:46.800
"And have you? Moved on?"
"Have you?"

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:51.280
Even in the second film, as Selene and&nbsp;
Michael finally consummate their relationship,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:55.840
the audience gets a scene that shows a lot&nbsp;
of skin, yet never bares much of anything.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:00.800
Unfortunately, Beckinsale generates more heat&nbsp;
by herself by talking about her feelings for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:05.360
Michael or interacting with his corpse when&nbsp;
she thinks he's dead late in the second movie

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:11.040
"Underworld: Rise of the Lycans" is a prequel&nbsp;
that explains the centuries-old origins of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:16.640
war between lycans and vampires focusing on&nbsp;
lycan Lucian and his forbidden relationship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:21.360
with vampire Sonja, which tragically results&nbsp;
in the latter being killed by her father and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:25.760
vampire leader Viktor when he discovers&nbsp;
that she's pregnant with a lycan child.

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:30.960
Yet, even if you haven't seen the third film&nbsp;
in the series, this story may sound familiar.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:36.320
That's because Lucien relates it in the first film&nbsp;
and, if that weren't enough, Michael experiences&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:41.600
it in a series of brief flashbacks. So while&nbsp;
"Rise of the Lycans" expands on the story, it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:46.160
still a rehash of a storyline that was summed up&nbsp;
in just a few minutes in the first "Underworld."

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:52.160
Alexander Corvinus passed the trait of eternal&nbsp;
life on to his twin sons Marcus and William,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:55.360
who became the first vampire&nbsp;
and werewolf, respectively.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.360 --> 00:03:00.400
While William was unable to assume his human&nbsp;
form ever again, the movie indicates Marcus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:04.560
became a vampire just like the others&nbsp;
presented in the franchise. That is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:09.520
until we meet him in "Underworld: Evolution"&nbsp;
and learn that he has giant bat wings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:14.960
the apparent result of being awoken from a lengthy&nbsp;
sleep by the blood of a slain lycan scientist.

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:20.080
Marcus spends a majority of the film flying around&nbsp;
and using his wings as weapons, but it's unclear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:25.920
why he has them. Early in the story, Selene tells&nbsp;
Michael he's the first vampire-lycan hybrid,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:30.880
and therefore there are no limits to what he&nbsp;
might be capable of. The question is why lycan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:36.800
blood would cause Marcus to sprout wings instead&nbsp;
of adopting more lycan-like traits. In the end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:41.040
it seems Marcus was given his winged&nbsp;
advantage because he's the first vampire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:43.600
but the movie never offers any real explanation.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:49.280
In most vampire properties, the species is&nbsp;
particularly vulnerable to wooden stakes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:53.920
through the heart and sunlight. The "Underworld"&nbsp;
franchise adheres to only half of that lore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:59.360
as the only thing that will definitely take out&nbsp;
this franchise's vampires is sunlight. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:03.680
vampires' vulnerability is so extreme&nbsp;
that their lycan enemies have learned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:08.320
to make UV bullets so they can destroy&nbsp;
vampires even when the sun is down.

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:13.680
Yet, while many vampires die from exposure to UV&nbsp;
light throughout the series, there are also many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:19.280
more deaths that aren't dependent on the sun.&nbsp;
For example, Viktor dies when Selene lobs off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:24.480
half of his head with a sword. Another elder,&nbsp;
Amelia, dies when she is drained of blood.

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:28.960
Although there's a certain logic to these&nbsp;
deaths, they're still somewhat surprising.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:33.760
More surprising still are the deaths of&nbsp;
two vampires in the series' second entry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:38.080
who Selene takes out by simply punching&nbsp;
them and throwing them against a wall.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:41.680
Given the strength and durability&nbsp;
this species is supposed to possess,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:45.680
it's hard to believe such a thing would&nbsp;
end the life of even the weakest vampire.

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:52.080
With the exception of "Underworld: Awakening," the&nbsp;
series takes place in an unnamed city in Eastern&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:56.880
Europe. From the looks of the language seen on&nbsp;
some of the signs, that city is likely in Hungary,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.880 --> 00:05:00.720
yet almost every character speaks&nbsp;
with an English or American accent.

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:05.360
"How ya doin'?"

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:10.320
Most puzzling of all, however, is the fact that&nbsp;
when we first meet Michael in "Underworld," he's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:16.400
clearly American, yet he's an intern at a local&nbsp;
hospital and the only co-worker he talks to is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:21.520
fellow American. But if Michael and his co-worker&nbsp;
want to be licensed doctors in the United States,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:26.320
they wouldn't do their internships in Eastern&nbsp;
Europe. Perhaps the films were supposed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:30.160
feel like they could take place anywhere, but&nbsp;
there's just enough evidence for them being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:35.760
set in a specific real-world location to make&nbsp;
the characters' accents extremely confusing.

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:40.800
From the opening scene of the first&nbsp;
"Underworld" one thing is abundantly clear:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:43.840
when vampire Death Dealers&nbsp;
find their lycan targets,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:47.920
their first response is to unleash a&nbsp;
barrage of bullets to take them down.

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:52.640
This would be expensive enough if they used&nbsp;
regular bullets, but because lycans are vulnerable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:57.920
to silver, they mostly employ specially-made&nbsp;
silver bullets, which would be even more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:03.520
costly. This means the vampires' budget for&nbsp;
their centuries-long war with the lycans must be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:07.520
massive. Given the expense and the need&nbsp;
to keep the war a secret from humans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:11.360
it's surprising the vampires on the front&nbsp;
lines of the battle weren't trained to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:16.320
conserve bullets by being more strategic&nbsp;
about where and when they fire. But instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:19.840
their philosophy seems to be shoot&nbsp;
first, and as much as possible.

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:25.440
"Underworld" features multiple immortal&nbsp;
fathers and their supernatural children,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:29.360
but there are two prominent examples&nbsp;
who present a sharp contrast.

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:34.080
On one hand, there's the original immortal,&nbsp;
Alexander Corvinus, whose sons became&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:39.680
the first vampire and werewolf. After Alexander&nbsp;
reveals he's spent his lengthy existence covering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:44.960
up the havoc his children have wreaked across the&nbsp;
centuries, he's asked why he didn't just kill his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:49.600
sons. But he acts like it would be impossible&nbsp;
for him, or any other father, to do such a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:55.200
thing. Despite this, his son Marcus demonstrates&nbsp;
he doesn't feel the same loyalty to his father,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.200 --> 00:07:00.160
given that a short time later he kills&nbsp;
Alexander while remarking on his cold heart.

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:03.200
On the other hand, there's&nbsp;
Viktor and his daughter Sonja.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:08.400
While Viktor initially seems to want to secure&nbsp;
a high place in vampire society for Sonja,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:12.880
he condemns her to death when he learns that&nbsp;
she's having an affair with the lycan Lucian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:17.760
and is pregnant with his child. Yet, Sonja's&nbsp;
supposed crime is far less horrific than those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:22.480
of Marcus and William.This is easy to overlook&nbsp;
while watching the films, but examining the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:27.600
two storylines side by side demonstrates the&nbsp;
warped priorities of the series' immortals.

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:33.680
Since its very first outing, the "Underworld"&nbsp;
franchise has employed a highly stylized,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:37.440
blue-filtered look. However,&nbsp;
there's one drawback to this choice:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:40.880
it makes it seem like the story&nbsp;
takes place entirely at night.

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:43.760
In the first "Underworld"&nbsp;
film, this was an advantage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.760 --> 00:07:47.840
since it just so happens that none of the&nbsp;
action was set during the day. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:52.960
in subsequent films, vampires' allergy to&nbsp;
the sun becomes an important plot point.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:58.560
Yet, in each instance, the films have to strain to&nbsp;
ensure the audience understands what's going on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:03.360
since it's challenging to interpret based on&nbsp;
what we're seeing, which is still very dark.

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:07.280
Nowhere is this more obvious than in&nbsp;
the third film, "Rise of the Lycans,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:11.440
which goes to great lengths to ensure&nbsp;
viewers understand the sun is rising.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.440 --> 00:08:16.160
Because of the visual palette chosen in the first&nbsp;
"Underworld" and maintained through the others,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:20.080
it is often impossible for audiences&nbsp;
to distinguish between day and night.

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:25.120
There are multiple clues to how vampire&nbsp;
society works that we can glean during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:29.840
the series from the way the creatures conduct&nbsp;
themselves. First, the vampires live together&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:34.880
in one location as a coven. In "Underworld,"&nbsp;
it's clear there are at least two covens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:39.360
although the information presented in later&nbsp;
films confirms there are actually more.

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:42.960
Between the authoritarian-like&nbsp;
leadership and insistence that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:47.280
everyone live together in order to ensure&nbsp;
they can be controlled and ordered around,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:52.640
it seems vampire society hasn't changed in&nbsp;
centuries, even as the world has moved on.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.640 --> 00:08:58.400
At one point, Selene comments that vampires don't&nbsp;
change, yet when it comes to clothes and fighting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.400 --> 00:09:03.680
her leather outfit and big guns indicate&nbsp;
that in some ways vampires have evolved. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:08.720
why hasn't vampires' style of living and&nbsp;
leadership changed at least the teensiest bit?

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:13.840
Viktor's lie about who truly killed&nbsp;
Selene's family is only one of many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:18.000
deceptions and omissions of truth that&nbsp;
drive the plots of the "Underworld" films.

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:26.080
"Help him? Of course not."
"Are you lying to me?"

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:30.880
In fact, there are so many characters&nbsp;
keeping secrets, often for centuries,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:36.080
that it becomes easy to forget just how much&nbsp;
the series hinges on various falsehoods,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:40.960
like Kraven's claim he killed Lucian and&nbsp;
his and Lucian's subsequent alliance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.960 --> 00:09:46.000
or Thomas never telling his son David that&nbsp;
his mother is the vampire elder Amelia.

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:50.640
So while supernatural creatures certainly&nbsp;
have a lot to hide from the human population,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:55.280
in "Underworld" the vampires and lycans find&nbsp;
plenty of reasons to hide things from one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:59.600
another as well, often for selfish reasons&nbsp;
that typically come back to haunt them.

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:05.360
The leather catsuit Kate Beckinsale wears&nbsp;
in the "Underworld" films has become iconic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:10.160
The irony is that Selene's chosen fighting&nbsp;
uniform is completely impractical for any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:14.000
kind of actual fighting. While the leather&nbsp;
will certainly prevent her from getting hurt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:19.280
too badly if she takes a tumble, that doesn't&nbsp;
seem like it would be a huge concern. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:23.440
her vampire healing should be enough&nbsp;
to ward off any issues if she falls.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:27.280
On the other hand, the leather in her&nbsp;
suit will only constrict her movements,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:32.480
overheat her, and make so much noise that it would&nbsp;
be very easy to hear her sneaking up behind you.

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:36.240
Of course, Selene is a vampire,&nbsp;
so it's possible she doesn't feel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:39.920
extreme temperatures, and she's strong&nbsp;
enough to overcome any limitations of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:43.920
the catsuit's leather. But Selene&nbsp;
is also a professional Death Dealer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:48.080
so it seems likely she would want to choose&nbsp;
clothing that would best support her work.

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:51.280
In the "Underworld" franchise, there are at least&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.280 --> 00:10:54.960
three separate occasions where a&nbsp;
female vampire becomes pregnant.

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:59.600
First, after having an affair with Lucian,&nbsp;
Sonja becomes pregnant. Then in the fourth film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:03.680
Selene is awoken after being held&nbsp;
for 12 years in a government facility&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:08.080
by the daughter she didn't know she was&nbsp;
pregnant with when she was captured. Finally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:13.680
in the fifth film, it's revealed that David's&nbsp;
mother was actually the vampire elder Amelia.

00:11:13.680 --> 00:11:18.800
When Sonja revealed her pregnancy, she claimed it&nbsp;
was a "miracle," but given how often it comes up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:24.480
in the franchise, it seems vampire pregnancy is,&nbsp;
in fact, possible. Although, like so many other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:29.120
things in these movies, the filmmakers seem&nbsp;
to be loath to provide additional information

